      "id": 145411,
      "name": "seesome",
      "username": "seesome",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/seesome/{size}/2018_2.png",
      "created_at": "2015-07-29T18:48:48.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>I was testing this further to see if I could replicated it as I didn't get screenshots thie first time.&nbsp; I've now reproduced it without the Meteor Swarm, although in both cases it involved a Start-of-Turn (SoT) question about skipping a turn for the Self-Destruct Sequence (SDS) and a SoT question for Bunker (e.g. destroy a mode? or load the omni-cannon?). This time, I captured screenshots of the whole sequence…</p><p><a href=\"http://i.imgur.com/P1DGUgx.jpg\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">Pic1</a>: Bunker's SoT, 3 cards under SDS – SDS asks about skipping B's turn &amp; I say yes</p><p><a href=\"http://i.imgur.com/yQ1nXTX.jpg\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">Pic2</a>: Legacy's SoT, 4 cards under SDS – SDS asks about skipping L's turn &amp; I say no</p><p><a href=\"http://i.imgur.com/nmcipXz.jpg\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">Pic3</a>: During L's turn, I click rewind and am given the option of going to B's SoT, Play a Card or Use a Power Phase; only B's SoT should be available as a valid choice. Interestingly, B's Draw a Card and End of Turn Phases aren't presented as options.</p><p><a href=\"http://i.imgur.com/JmucdCR.jpg\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">Pic4</a>: I rewind to B's Play a Card Phase and can continue his turn. Note that there are still 4 cards under the SDS.</p><p>FYI, If I chose to rewind to B's SoT, it would reset this sequence to the beginning and I could replicate it.</p><p>[I Xposted these details &amp; screenshots to the Handleabra forum as well]</p><p>&nbsp;</p>",
