      "read": false,
      "user_title": null,
      "bookmarked": false,
      "raw": "<p>I was testing this further to see if I could replicated it as I didn&#39;t get screenshots thie first time.&nbsp; I&#39;ve now reproduced it without the Meteor Swarm, although in both cases it involved a Start-of-Turn (SoT) question about skipping a turn for the Self-Destruct Sequence (SDS) and a SoT question for Bunker (e.g. destroy a mode? or load the omni-cannon?). This time, I captured screenshots of the whole sequence&hellip;</p><p><a href=\"http://i.imgur.com/P1DGUgx.jpg\">Pic1</a>: Bunker&#39;s SoT, 3 cards under SDS &ndash; SDS asks about skipping B&#39;s turn &amp; I say yes</p><p><a href=\"http://i.imgur.com/yQ1nXTX.jpg\">Pic2</a>: Legacy&#39;s SoT, 4 cards under SDS &ndash; SDS asks about skipping L&#39;s turn &amp; I say no</p><p><a href=\"http://i.imgur.com/nmcipXz.jpg\">Pic3</a>: During L&#39;s turn, I click rewind and am given the option of going to B&#39;s SoT, Play a Card or Use a Power Phase; only B&#39;s SoT should be available as a valid choice. Interestingly, B&#39;s Draw a Card and End of Turn Phases aren&#39;t presented as options.</p><p><a href=\"http://i.imgur.com/JmucdCR.jpg\">Pic4</a>: I rewind to B&#39;s Play a Card Phase and can continue his turn. Note that there are still 4 cards under the SDS.</p><p>FYI, If I chose to rewind to B&#39;s SoT, it would reset this sequence to the beginning and I could replicate it.</p><p>[I Xposted these details &amp; screenshots to the Handleabra forum as well]</p><p>&nbsp;</p>",
